GREEN ON BRANCH print-reshape (SEQ 449 R4). Three things stood between FORMAt and a printed format, each measured:
1. FORMAt never matched a plain `#d`: a set term that matches ZERO characters (`flags=[-# 0+']*`) fails the rule. It
   matched `#0d` and not `#d`. Cure: `flags?=[-# 0+']+` (optional, one or more). The old grammar's FormaT has the same
   spelling; it is not reached there in today's tree (a `#` after an expression is a StringXP).
2. PRECISIOn's `dot='.'` crashed every format at parse (exit 139, PLGset::set on a null set in ensureGuard): the quoted
   '.' resolves to the `.` OPERATOR field, whose guard is null. Cure: `dot=[.]`, digits `precision?=[0-9]+`. Same
   latent crash in the old grammar's Precision.
3. printField applies no format on EITHER road in today's tree: tok's `print(buffer) gCount` generates
   appendInt(gCount,0,0) and ignores `format`. CORRECTED (Tony, SEQ 450 R2): formats worked once; grammar changes broke
   them; the date is not measured -- this file first said they had never worked. printFormatted now applies one when it is handed in (only opPrintList hands one); with none,
   printField is byte for byte as before, so the old road is unmoved (printPop identical).
